# Edge Functions

- Use Deno-compatible TypeScript and kebab-case function directories.
- Keep shared utilities in `_shared`; every deployable function has its own pinned `deno.json`.
- Parse and validate every request before use. Return intentional status codes and safe error bodies.
- Read provider credentials from `Deno.env.get`; fail safely when they are missing and never log secrets or tokens.
- Keep external calls bounded with timeouts where available. Handlers that may retry must be idempotent.
- Use structured logs with request IDs and non-sensitive context only.
- Give handlers and helpers one cohesive responsibility; extract only independently
  meaningful or testable responsibilities, not merely to meet a line count.
- Keep equal explicit inputs and dependencies deterministic whenever feasible. Pass
  time, randomness, external state, concurrency, and I/O through an appropriate
  explicit boundary; bound and validate variation where applicable, and test or
  document observable behavior. Do not use hidden mutable state or incidental
  nondeterminism.
